{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And commits a trespass against HaShem.</b> That he transgressed a negative commandment in a matter between him and another person." "<b>Or in a matter of deposit.</b> A partnership in which he placed his hand with him." "<b>Robbery.</b> By force, as in 'and he seized the spear' [2 Samuel 23:21]." "<b>Oppression.</b> In secret." "<b>And his fellow.</b> His fellow. And it is possible that it is עומתו (opposite him). And the heh is added in place of [the preposition]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:42.749279838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}